  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Skittering Horror" id="5644-27ad-e862-118b" hidden="false">
      <description>This unit can move over terrain as if it had the *airborne* keyword.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explosive End (2”)" id="e7a2-d585-bc1b-637d" hidden="false">
      <description>When this unit is destroyed, before removing the model, roll a dice. On a 5+, it explodes in a blast attack, with a 2” radius originating from its base, with a strength of +3 and a damage of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Explosive End (D5&quot;)" id="5d45-8796-2e04-09ea" hidden="false">
      <description>When this unit is destroyed, before removing the model, it explodes in a 3” blast radius from its base, with a strength of +3 and a damage of 1. If this unit was destroyed by a *psychic* attack, the explosion has a damage of 2, and counts as a psychic *attack*.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hyperion Armour" id="4b7d-f9db-3dbe-36e3" hidden="false">
      <description>Attacks with a damage characteristic of 2 or less that target this unit are made with disadvantage.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Kastellite" id="6201-4fa2-fb10-052b" hidden="false">
      <description>The rules for this unit are provided hereas a demonstration for future, and players that wish to use it may replace one *Construct* unit in a warband with this unit.
However, as it is part of a very distinct subfaction, it will be available solely in a unique warband when therestof its subfaction is released.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
